    dynamic_reserve_requirements: { cell: "R", ev: "neiso-57 — NOT PROMOTED pending an owner decision rather than refuted; it engages, is a measured market-design input with zero fitted parameters, and produced the model's first structurally-formed scarcity hour. RE-SIZED 2026-09-17 (neiso-111) AGAINST A DIFFERENT TARGET (the C3c tail), which is new evidence rather than a rule-28(a) re-test — and the sizing is NEGATIVE ALONE and partly the WRONG WAY. Measured ISO-NE ROS (location 7000) at Elliott, Dec 23-26 2022: 10-min SPIN mean 384.0 MW against the model's static 600 (a LOOSENING of -212.0 MW), 10-min TOTAL 1,533.7 vs static 1,200 (+349.8), 30-min TOTAL 2,337.4 vs static 1,800 (+554.1). The published columns are NESTED (spin subset of ten-minute subset of TOTAL: 388 <= 1,549.8 <= 2,354.1), while the model runs three SEPARATE balance rows whose statics sum to 3,600 MW — so measured against the model's aggregate posture the mechanism is a 1,246 MW LOOSENING, not the +500 MW tightening the neiso-111 charter assumed. Per family the increments land against a class-0 supply of 6,959.1 MW and class-1 of 5,217.5 MW at Elliott and come nowhere near binding. It DOES cross when paired with supply-side response scoping (scoped class-0 2,271.6 MW vs measured 2,354.1 MW = short 82.5 MW), so it is a COMPLEMENT, never a standalone. BLOCKER (a) IS FALSIFIED: the raw payload is absent from disk (README only) and its stated 2023-2025 coverage policy cites rule 22 [R-HOLDOUT], REMOVED 2026-09-09; the ISO Express report was probed live from the session container and returned 2020 and 2022 windows successfully through the committed downloader's isox_token bootstrap (a bare curl 403s, which is not the blocker it looks like). neiso-57's summer-tail objection is UNTOUCHED and still stands. docs/FINDING-neiso111-reserve-supply-scoping-2026-09-17.md section 4." },
