    reserve_deliverability_scoping: { cell: "U", ev: "\".\" -> U 2026-09-17 (neiso-111), a rule 28(d) TRANSFER CANDIDATE entering NEISO untested — no NEISO field exists yet, and NO NEISO PARAMETER IS CARRIED FROM ANY OTHER ISO (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]). Why NEISO is NOT the PJM/CAISO/MISO case this row already adjudicates INERT: those closed because their reserve headroom ran 9.7-15x the requirement, and NEISO's does not. MEASURED, zero LP, from the neiso-110 screen bundle unit_hourly_2022 (sha 7b82a4c08039c04f348884dfad894e196a9a16fb) at the Elliott minimum-headroom hour 8633 (2022-12-26 17:00): class-0 headroom 6,959.1 MW is 73.3 MW ONLINE (1.05%, 281 units) and 6,885.8 MW OFFLINE (98.95%, 329 units). _neiso_design gates eligibility on FUEL NAME ALONE (_reserve_eligible / _quick_start_eligible) with no start-time, ramp or online test, so 2,855.2 MW of oil-fired STEAM BOILERS (EIA-860 generator prime mover ST, 100% of oil units matched) count as ISO-NE TEN-MINUTE reserve in every hour of the year — a rule 18 [R-PHYSICS] violation in form as well as substance. The LP already accepts online_gated / online_rho / online_capacity_cap / reserve_supply_cap / pergen_ramp10 and NEISO passes none of them. SIZING, NOT A PREDICTION: strictest-admissible scoping leaves class-1 supply >= 1,494.9 MW in all 8,760 hours of 2022 against a 1,200 MW requirement (ZERO short hours — the scoping alone produces no scarcity hour, the same shape as neiso-110's derate result), and crosses only when paired with the measured requirement, by 82.5 MW. A correctly designed mechanism will be LOOSER than that measurement and may not cross. docs/FINDING-neiso111-reserve-supply-scoping-2026-09-17.md sections 5-6." },
