    coal_fuel_inventory: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-16 (miso-259) WITH the field \u2014 U: UNTESTED here, and the field RAISES rather than silently skipping if armed for this ISO. The chartering measurement is MISO's own coal stock and receipts footprint; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean MISO's verdict fills no other ISO's cell. The datatypes are NATIONAL and the read-time join is ISO-agnostic, so a coal ISO arming this needs no new intake \u2014 but it must derive its own footprint, its own delivery-rate construction and its own shared-storage reconciliation from its own market's data, and lift the MISO gate deliberately." },
    hydro_pondage_bound: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-20 (hydro-1) WITH the field (rule 28c). UNTESTED for this ISO: no data/raw/<iso>-hydro/<iso>_hydro_pondage.csv artifact exists at HEAD, so data/hydro.py::load_hydro_pondage returns None, the shared resolver returns UNSET and the LP is byte-identical. A lane that wants this ISO tested derives its own artifact from its own dams (scripts/data/build_hydro_pondage.py) — no number crosses an ISO boundary (rule 25)." },
  hydro_cascade_coupling: { cell: ".", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-16 (NWPP-36) WITH the field \u2014 n/a for this ISO at HEAD: no <iso>_hydro_cascade_{links,monthly}.csv artifact exists, so data/hydro.py::load_hydro_cascade returns None, pipeline/kwargs.py::resolve_hydro_cascade returns UNSET and the dispatch-kwargs key set and LP are unchanged (byte-identical, measured: this ISO's keeper cache_key unmoved base 6d1a144d -> head). Rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): NWPP's measurement fills no other ISO's cell; an ISO with a measured hydraulic chain (a CROHMS-class hourly project feed, a dam inventory with surface areas, EIA-923 plant-months) enters as U and derives its own tau / band / eta / inflow from its own river." },
