    chp_steam_duty_window: { cell: "U", ev: "row minted with the field 2026-09-20 (caiso-293, rule 28c). UNTESTED HERE. The mechanism is ISO-GENERIC in FORM — data/fleet/arrays.py's MECH_CHP_STEAM block runs for every ISO and the loader reads whatever thermal-tranche artifact the ISO has — and the measured footprint is nonzero wherever the ISO carries status==ok CHP rows (G-1 census: NYISO per-unit 17, CAISO 13, NWPP 7, SOCO 5, SPP 3; MISO/NEISO/PJM/NYISO-pooled 0, so those artifacts cannot reach it at all today). Rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]: CAISO's evidence transfers to NOBODY — this cell opens only on this ISO's own measured conduct, and CAISO's own arm STOPPED at its pre-registered G-4 (see the CAISO shard) so there is nothing here worth transferring yet. Default off, byte-identical off; this ISO's keeper is unchanged and unaffected." },
