    energy_online_capability_cap: { cell: "." },
    offer_curve_by_group: { cell: "K", ev: "STAYS K, MAGNITUDE RE-DERIVED. neiso-106 (2026-09-06) re-sized the scalar this cell carries from 0.93391 (a 6.609% cut) to 0.95470 (4.530%) and promoted it as keeper 2026-09-06-neiso-106-fossil-offer -- the SAME 12 markup bands, the SAME channel, the SAME target, so no verdict moves and no lever is opened. Only the COEFFICIENT in the sizing division changed: from the neiso-104 screen's ONE-YEAR pass-through 0.5247 to the full-span 0.76550 measured directly off the neiso-105 keeper's own three in-sample price moves. Landing, pre-registered before the solve and hit to 0.02 pp on every year: C3a 2023 -1.34%, 2024 +1.76%, 2025 -0.77%; in-sample geometric-mean bias -0.124% against a predicted -0.119%; MAE 1.290%. Identity re-checked on the arm's own run_config: exactly 12 bands moved, all at ratio 0.954700, zero out-of-scope, every phys_*/peak/econ_low_share/pct_peaking bit-identical to the pre-cut neiso-99 base. Footprint re-checked: largest out-of-scope class move 0.0017 TWh against ~114 TWh of load. TWO MEASUREMENTS THIS CELL NOW CARRIES THAT IT DID NOT BEFORE, both cheap to reuse in any ISO. (i) PASS-THROUGH IS YEAR-DEPENDENT, NOT DEPTH-DEPENDENT: 1.3055 / 0.9525 / 0.8138 / 0.7061 / 0.5269 / 0.4126 across 2020 / 2023 / 2024 / 2021 / 2025 / 2022, monotonically INVERSE in delivered gas; and 2025 measured at TWO cut depths gives 0.5254 at 4.53% against 0.5269 at 6.609%, ratio 1.0029 -- so the depth-linearity hazard PREREG-neiso105 section 3 named is refuted and a coefficient measured at one depth may be reused at another. (ii) THE neiso-104 REFUTATION WAS A SCREEN-YEAR ARTIFACT, NOT A COEFFICIENT ERROR: the across-year gas elasticity 0.765 this cell recorded as REFUTED is 0.7655 on the full span, right to within 0.07%; rule 29's largest-footprint screen-year rule had selected the lowest-pass-through year. Filed as an owner ask, not acted on. Bit-level cross-check: this arm's 2025 solve reproduces the DELETED neiso-104 screen arm exactly (P0 objective 3,554,608,783.6457, 188,740 / 59,473 simplex iterations on both passes) across four package version deltas. Evidence: FINDING-neiso106-offer-level-rederived-2026-09-06.md; PREREG-neiso106-offer-level-rederived-2026-09-06.md; ADDENDUM-neiso106-prereg-collision-2026-09-06.md; _neiso106_offer_level_phase0.json. || PRIOR EVIDENCE, preserved: STAYS K — armed on the keeper and NOT adjudicated by the neiso-104 screen, which killed its own arm without touching the mechanism's standing (rule 32b: a tested mechanism is stamped even when the arm dies). neiso-104 (2026-09-06) screened the rules 1/13 authorized price-tuning channel on 2025: a single declared scalar 0.9547 (4.53% cut) on 12 MARKUP bands (committed/econ_low/econ_high of CC_REGULAR, CC_CHP, CT_PEAKER, ST_GAS), sized ex ante as the in-sample 2023-25 geometric-mean price bias 0.0347 / a measured across-year gas elasticity 0.765, owner-selected estimator, declared in PREREG-neiso104-fossil-offer-level-2026-09-06.md before any solve. THE MECHANISM BEHAVED EXACTLY AS SPECIFIED and that is why the cell does not move: G2 footprint PASS (largest out-of-scope class move 0.0050 TWh against ~114 TWh load; nuclear/wind/solar/hydro/interchange 0.0000) and G3 identity PASS (exactly 12 bands moved; all four peak bands, every phys_*, econ_low_share and pct_peaking bit-identical). WHAT FAILED WAS THE SIZING MODEL, NOT THE CHANNEL: G1 STOP at a delivered -2.38% price move against a pre-registered -3.47%, off by 1.09 pp on a +/-1.0 pp tolerance, i.e. a REALIZED PASS-THROUGH OF 0.525 against the declared 0.765 — below even the within-year elasticity 0.593 the PREREG argued against. That trips PREREG section 7's pre-committed trigger (<0.60 => stop and re-derive) and THE SCALAR WAS NOT RAISED: back-solving 4.53% x 0.765/0.525 ~ 6.6% from the screen is the rule 1 condition (c) sweep and is neither done nor proposed. The full span was NOT spent; no successor arm is pre-registered. 2020 was never this lane's object and lands at +11.00% on the measured move (PREREG section 3.3 had pre-registered its verdict as UNDETERMINED; the screen resolves it to the failing side) — rule 30(c) untouched, NEISO's determination remains its train-tier CALIBRATED. COLLATERAL RESULT, recorded because it governs future control spending in this ISO: the same-HEAD control REPRODUCED THE COMMITTED KEEPER to 4 dp on load-weighted price ($71.3866 vs $71.3866) and to 0.001 TWh on every class (0.0000 TWh summed absolute difference) despite 111 live-candidate files / 28,119 changed lines on the NEISO backcast path since the keeper git_sha b7904a1, AND despite four environment deltas (highspy 1.14.0 -> 1.15.1, pandas 3.0.3 -> 3.0.5, pydantic 2.13.4 -> 2.13.5, kernel v20 -> v24) — CORRECTED 2026-09-06 by ADDENDUM-neiso104-env-correction-2026-09-06.md, which retracts this stamp's original wording 'BIT-IDENTICALLY' and this session's separate claim that the replay environment matched the keeper's exactly: the environment did NOT match (the driver printed the deltas before solving and they were not read) and no per-cell comparison was run, so the result holds at the two tolerances stated and not at bit-identity; it is STRONGER for having survived the environment deltas but is stated more weakly because that is what was measured, and cannot be tightened without a re-solve since both bundles were deleted under rule 29(c) — so THE KEEPER IS NOT STALE and G-CTRL form 4 was valid all along, the control solve being unnecessary in hindsight though correct to spend ex ante (data/offer_curves.py, the channel's own consumption path, had moved 391 lines and a path-name triage is not a hunk audit). Two rule-mechanics collisions filed, not worked around: screen gate G4 is NOT EVALUABLE because calibration_verdict.py resolves only a REGISTERED run while rule 29(2) forbids registering a screen bundle (no substitute verdict was hand-rolled); and G-DRIFT's 'costs seconds' premise degrades with keeper age. Both screen bundles DELETED before merge (rule 29(c)); the FINDING is the record. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-neiso104-offer-level-screen-2026-09-06.md; prereg PREREG-neiso104-fossil-offer-level-2026-09-06.md; drift audit ADDENDUM-neiso104-gdrift-2026-09-06.md; declared bands _neiso104_arm_offer_curve.json; phase 0 _neiso104_offer_level_phase0.json" },
