    measured_chp_heat_rates: { cell: "K", ev: "neiso-70 (results/calibration/FINDING-neiso70-heat-rate-provenance-2026-07-31.md); successor CLOSED at neiso-71 (results/calibration/FINDING-neiso71-chp-floor-nuclear-2026-07-31.md); capacity prerequisite ADJUDICATED-ARTIFACT at neiso-73 (results/calibration/FINDING-neiso73-kendall-capacity-basis-2026-07-31.md); PROMOTED TO KEEPER at neiso-81 (2026-08-04): prereg results/calibration/PREREG-neiso81-chp-heat-rate-readjudication-2026-08-04.md (pushed before either arm solved), finding results/calibration/FINDING-neiso81-chp-heat-rate-promotion-2026-08-04.md, A/B record results/calibration/_neiso81_chpheatrate_ab.json, Phase-0 results/calibration/_neiso81_chp_phase0.json, arms 2026-08-04-neiso81-control / -chpheatrate; ARTIFACT RE-DERIVED UNDER SCOPE GATE 3 at neiso-80 (2026-08-04, NO LP, keeper unchanged) — THE CELL DOES NOT MOVE AND STAYS O, an input correction with no mechanism surface (the caiso-156/159 precedent). NEISO's chp_power_only_heat_rates artifact was the last of the three dark-fuel-carrying ISOs still written PRE-gate-3 (19 columns, no dark_fuel_share; miso-122 re-derived only MISO's and nyiso-120 only NYISO's, each handing NEISO's off with a number under rule 25). Re-derived at --vintage 2023, every pre-registered property holds: P1 CONSUMPTION (the artifact has exactly ONE caller, campd_bins.measured_chp_heat_rates -> chp.apply_measured_chp_heat_rates -> eia860.py:1686, gated on the flag), P2 STRICT NO-OP (six frozen columns bit-identical on all 40 rows; only (1595, CC_CHP) heat_rate moves and only downward; flag census unchanged 22/12/5/1), P3 MAGNITUDE REPRODUCES TO 4 dp (dark_fuel_share 0.012142, heat_rate 9.5584 -> 9.4423), P4 RECONCILIATION (cems_vs_egrid_total 1.0, in the (0.9,1.1) band, flag stays ok), P5 NO CROSS-ISO WRITE (exactly one file changed). THE GATE IS A STABLE PHYSICAL FEATURE, NOT A ONE-YEAR ARTIFACT: measured on NEISO's own CAMPD at unit grain the dark share is 0.012142 / 0.009584 / 0.014798 for 2023/2024/2025 (corrected rate 9.4423 / 9.4668 / 9.4170), reproducing the hand-off series 1.21/0.96/1.48 % exactly; the committed artifact is the 2023 vintage so 9.4423 is the number of record and the other two are stability evidence only (no vintage mixing). SCORE-INERT ON THE DESIGNATED KEEPER BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT BY MEASUREMENT: the keeper's run_config records measured_chp_heat_rates=false, so the artifact is not read on its solve path at all and NO solve is owed. CEILING MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED, and pre-declared before the derive ran: over the repriced population (12 rows, 429.7 MW) the seam dearness goes +36.08 % -> +35.31 % (CC_CHP only, 3 rows / 378.2 MW: +36.72 % -> +35.81 %), i.e. the gate walks back 2.15 % — about one part in forty-six — of the seam move that produced the neiso-70 CC_CHP overshoot. IT CANNOT AND DOES NOT FLIP THE CELL, and was never offered as a route; the O blocker is unchanged (the missing host-steam obligation, itself closed by neiso-71 as a REAL FLEET DIFFERENCE — NEISO's merchant CC_CHP genuinely carries none — whose DO-NOT-REDO stands). RULE 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE] citation: the miso-122 gate-3 SCOPE CHANGE on measured grounds, never a residual; rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] governs in both directions and no residual was consulted (nor could be, per P1). HAND-OFF UNCHANGED IN KIND (rule 25): PJM's and CAISO's artifacts remain un-gated at 19 columns and miso-122 measured both at < 0.1 % dark fuel, so their expected rate movement is zero — but that is THEIR lanes' measurement and NO PJM or CAISO cell is stamped. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-neiso80-chp-scope-gate-and-steam-part-2026-08-04.md; prereg PREREG-neiso80-chp-scope-gate-and-steam-part-2026-08-04.md" },
