    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "K", ev: "KEEPER (neiso-fuelvintage-1, 2026-09-09; owner ruling of the same day, verbatim: \'these should be promoted as keepers on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness\'). ARMED in the promoted NEISO keeper recipe and MEASURED PROVABLY INERT there, at zero LP, before any solve (rule 29 [R-SCREEN] clause (0)). The census builds the NEISO fleet twice per year through run_year(fleet_only=True) on the keeper own meta.json, differing only in this flag (scripts/probes/_neiso_fuelvintage_census.py): 2023/2024/2025 give 7,665,000 + 7,577,400 + 7,594,920 = 22,837,320 fuel cells with ZERO written, max |delta| exactly 0.0 on both fuel_prices and mc_base, and a full-payload sweep of all 38 arrays run_year returns (38,518,653 numeric cells) finds NOT ONE that differs. So the LP is literally the same LP and the promotion cannot move a criterion. WHY: the FINDING-xiso-fuelvintage-monthly-gas-level-2026-09-09 section 4 ordering working as designed -- the solve own log reads 'hub-basis overlay (NEISO 2023, daily): 463 gas generators repriced at the measured hub spot in 12/12 months', so gas_hub_basis_overlay (Algonquin Citygate via the ISO-NE MA index) supersedes the state-average seam in every gas cell of every month, and gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing overwrites from F923 prints on top. The LP screen the handoff scheduled for this cell was CANCELLED, not skipped: an LP whose inputs are proven bit-identical cannot produce a different output. THE PHASE-0 DISCREPANCY THIS CELL CARRIED IS NOW SETTLED and the earlier 'stated not proven' reading is PROVEN -- docs/FINDING-neiso-index-vs-delivered-gas-2026-09-09.md. The Jan-2023 3.24x gap (ISO-NE AGT index 4.73 vs N3045 MA/CT/RI/ME/NH blend 15.35 $/MMBtu) is a MEASUREMENT-BASIS GAP -- an average delivered cost including transportation and contract (LNG) charges versus the marginal commodity price -- and the delivered series is falsified AS A MARGINAL PRICE physically: over 84 months (2019-01..2025-12) the implied marginal heat rate (monthly mean ISO-NE hub RT LMP / gas price) never once falls below 7.99 MMBtu/MWh on the index, while the N3045 blend drives it below the 6.3 MMBtu/MWh CC floor in 13 of 84 months and to 3.29 in Jan-2023 -- a ~104%-efficient heat engine. Corroborated: N3045 prices Jan-2023 and Jan-2025 the same (15.346 vs 15.316) while the market priced them 50.51 vs 135.08 $/MWh and gas ran HARDER in the cheap month (49.3% vs 46.8% share); the Algonquin daily prints read 3.22-4.23 for four weeks of Jan-2023; and MA/CT dispersion inside one month reaches 4.13x on the same pipeline, which the COMMODITY cannot do but an AVERAGE DELIVERED COST can (firm-transport charges and Everett LNG; Massachusetts is the state that prints high). CORRECTED BEFORE PUBLICATION, recorded rather than quietly fixed: an earlier draft called this a RESPONDENT-COMPOSITION artifact, on the strength of this repository's EIA-923 receipt EXTRACTION holding a single New England plant that month (1660 Potter Station 2, 58 MW, 28,703 MMBtu). That is a property of the EXTRACTION, not of EIA's respondent set: the parallel session neiso-107 measured EIA's companion VOLUME series N3045<ST>2 at 1.6% of the CAMPD-metered burn (36/36 months of 2022-2024 inside a 0.32 MMBtu/MWh implied-heat-rate band), and their metered leg reproduces EXACTLY here at 29,290,427 MMBtu. The mechanism is corrected; the verdict and every other line of evidence are unchanged. Log-price correlation with realised LMP: index 0.9324, N3045 0.8452. CONSEQUENCE: rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] misalignment exception is EARNED, not merely invoked -- the hub index keeps priority because it is the marginal series, and the 2.303 $/MMBtu level gap the cross-ISO table reports for NEISO 2023 measures the survey panel, NOT the model. RECOMMENDED AGAINST (not built): an ercot-261-style corroborator for NEISO -- the second series fails a physical test, so corroborating against it would import panel noise into the series that is already marginal. CROSS-CORROBORATED INDEPENDENTLY: the parallel NEISO session neiso-107 ran this same task on the same handoff and proved the SAME inertness by its own zero-LP A/B, and reached the SAME verdict on the gas question -- it recorded this cell as I (inert). The cell reads K here, not I, because the OWNER RULING of 2026-09-09 ('promoted as keepers ... regardless of inertness') WITHDREW the leave-the-flag-off guidance neiso-107 was following: the mechanism IS armed in the designated keeper's recipe, which is what K means, and its measured inertness is reported as a property of the result rather than as a reason to withhold. Both readings of the MEASUREMENT agree exactly; only the DISPOSITION differs, and the later ruling settles it. neiso-107's evidence is preserved at docs/FINDING-neiso-gas-index-vs-delivered-2026-09-09.md, and its N3045 VOLUME test is what corrected this lane's first (wrong) mechanism -- see the CORRECTED BEFORE PUBLICATION note above." },
