    gas_coldsnap_derate: { cell: "K" },
    coldsnap_derate_dualfuel_conditional: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-16 (session neiso-110, owner ruling: 'Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper.'). Keeper 2026-09-16-neiso110-dualfuel-derate-scope, the neiso-109 recipe replayed FULL SPAN 2020-2025 with exactly this one field flipped. PROMOTED FOR STRUCTURAL FIDELITY UNDER RULE 1 [R-STRUCT], NEVER ON THE RESIDUAL, and the full span CONFIRMS the screen's verdict rather than overturning it: the arm closes 0.01/0.05/0.10/0.01/0.00/0.02 % of the oil gap in 2020-2025 (+0.00154 TWh total). Nothing regresses -- C3a improves in 5 of 6 years (2020 moves 0.028 pp the other way), every move <0.09 pp; slack/dump delta 0.0000 all six years; hours >$300 = 0 in BOTH legs all six years; the reserve co-opt stays dormant (0 nonzero duals in 26,280 family-hours per year, both legs); D1/D2/D4 statuses identical; largest non-oil class move 0.0033 TWh. DETERMINATION UNCHANGED at CALIBRATED with the same single ledgered C3c caveat. DOF ledger UNCHANGED (n_entries 8 / n_residual 6): a scope condition adds no free parameter, and the parent derate's t0/slope/cap are byte-identical so rule 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE] is not engaged. THE PRIOR R VERDICT IS NOT ERASED -- it was correct and it still stands as the finding about OIL: this mechanism is NOT the fix for NEISO's winter oil burn, and the DO-NOT-REDO below still binds. What changed is only the disposition: a structurally-correct correction is kept because it is correct. THE SCREEN RECORD, PRESERVED VERBATIM: TESTED AND REFUTED AS THE OIL FIX -- but the DEFECT IT NAMES STANDS. neiso-110 screen (2026-09-16, ONE LP on 2022, keeper UNCHANGED, remaining five years NOT spent per rule 29 [R-SCREEN]). Screen year 2022 named in PRECOMMIT-neiso110-coldsnap-dualfuel-2026-09-16.md BEFORE the solve, chosen on the MECHANISM'S OWN FOOTPRINT (164.1 GWh of capacity-hours reached, 2.5x the next year), a quantity carrying no residual term. Verdict RESULT-neiso110-coldsnap-dualfuel-screen-2026-09-16.md. THE MECHANISM FIRED EXACTLY AS SPECIFIED -- G1 PASSES to 0.37%: on the coldest derated day (doy 16, frac 0.18225) dual-fuel capacity reads 4,230.2 MW in-window against 5,154.2 MW out, ratio 0.82074 versus a predicted 0.81775. G6 PASSES (largest class move 0.00237% of ISO load; C3a -6.205% -> -6.120%, i.e. TOWARD the bench) and G7 PASSES (slack and dump 0.000000 in both legs). G2/G3/G4 hold by construction plus tests/iso/neiso/test_neiso_coldsnap_dualfuel_exemption.py -- NOT by bundle differencing, because the keeper bundle is slim and carries no unit_hourly to difference against; stated rather than glossed. G5 FAILS AND KILLS THE ARM: oil +1.32% and gas -0.00% against a pre-registered >10% non-triviality threshold. Oil moves +0.00172 TWh against a 1.72 TWh gap -- it closes 0.1%. Price mean 85.550 -> 85.628, max UNCHANGED at 249.47, hours >$300 STILL ZERO. WHY, MEASURED NOT INFERRED: the reserve co-opt stayed fully dormant in the arm exactly as in the control -- 0 nonzero duals in 26,280 family-hours, zero shortfall, held_mw still exactly on requirement. THE NUMBER THAT RETIRES THE WHOLE LEVER FAMILY: at Elliott the model's minimum thermal headroom is 6,959 MW against a 3,600 MW total reserve requirement, so it sits 3,359 MW clear of binding; this screen removed ~779 MW, and derating 100% OF ALL NEISO GAS (17,565 MW) would remove only 1,985 MW -- the physically maximal version of this entire mechanism falls ~40% short of producing ONE reserve-short hour. The documented chain (derate -> shortage -> RCPF -> >$300 tail -> oil clears) is broken at its FIRST link by a margin no admissible magnitude crosses. WHAT STANDS: the exemption is genuinely UNEARNED. The parent derate exempts 6,896 MW (39.3% of NEISO gas capacity) on the premise that apply_dual_fuel_pricing switched those units to oil; that switch is mc = min(gas, oil) and at Elliott gas ran $12.54-15.08/MMBtu against an oil parity of $20.985, so it was $5.9-8.4/MMBtu from firing. The code is correct, gated, default-off and byte-identical off; arming it buys CORRECTNESS, NOT ACCURACY, and the arm/merge decision is the owner's (RESULT section 7). DO-NOT-REDO (rule 28a): do not re-test this cell, and do not propose another cold-snap-derate magnitude lever for NEISO winter scarcity, without new evidence that addresses the 3,359 MW headroom directly. The lead routed instead is the DEMAND BOUNDARY -- the model serves 1,483.6 GWh across Elliott against a measured 1,711.6 GWh (~1,900 MW of load), though that gap is systematic (annual ratio 0.856 vs 0.867 at Elliott) and is probably a definitional imports/losses boundary rather than a miss." },
