    hindcast_verified_announced_exits: { cell: ".", fc: "I", ev: "NEISO fc U -> I at neiso-mystic-rescore (2026-08-22). ARMED AND MEASURED INERT, not assumed: the harness default carries hindcast_verified_announced_exits=true in this run's run_config.json, and the run's model output is BIT-IDENTICAL to neiso-2021-2025-realized-k99 (2026-08-19), which predates the field and ran without it -- retire total 7.332 GW and every per-fuel figure reproduce exactly (biomass 0.002 / coal 0.791 / gas_cc 5.100 / gas_ct 0.000 / gas_st 1.438 / oil 0.000). MECHANISM-LEVEL CONFIRMATION, independent of the solve: load_announced_reversal_plants('NEISO') returns the EMPTY SET under BOTH arms -- as_of=None (the un-gated verified arm) and as_of=2020-12-31 (the ex-ante arm) -- because NEISO's confirmed-retirements registry carries NO reversal row to un-gate. Its only two rows are Merrimack 1/2 (Clean Water Act consent decree, gsp-cwa-cd-merrimack-1/2), both superseded=False with a null superseding instrument, and both DOUBLE-BLOCKED in-window anyway: exit_year 2028 falls outside 2021-2025, and instrument_date 2024-03-29 post-dates the run's 2020-12-31 vintage cutoff. The flag therefore cannot change the NEISO fleet under any in-window configuration. Scope note: this is the INERTNESS verdict for NEISO ONLY (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]) -- the owner directive that minted the field came from a PJM nuclear false-retire investigation and no cell outside NEISO is stamped here. Evidence: docs/hindcast-reports/neiso-2021-2025-realized-mystic-rescore-2026-08-22.md (Provenance section); bundle results/hindcast/neiso-2021-2025-realized-mystic-rescore/NEISO/e118e887b306da37." },
