    mass_cap_schedule: { cell: ".", fc: "O", ev: "SCN-CAP (2026-09-06): field + CAP-STATE-TIGHT case landed for every ISO (rule 28c); NEISO UNTESTED — a zero-LP build lane, nothing solved. Zero-LP phase 0 from the committed pre-D77 REF (FINDING §3): the S12 schedule (20.67 -> 18.0 Mt) is SLACK on NEISO in every year 2026-2030 by 2.9-4.8 Mt against REF 15.8 -> 13.4 Mt, so under the charter's rule case 13 is KILLED at phase 0 on NEISO, never solved — byte-identical to REF (row built, dual 0); a post-D77 REF cannot flip it. Backcast lane '.' by construction (rule 13: coerced to None in backcast/hindcast). Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-scn-cap-2026-09-06.md SCN-WS5A-POLICY-NEISO (2026-09-07) SOLVES IT AND THE PRIOR CELL TEXT IS CORRECTED: fc U -> O. THE CLAIM ABOVE THAT CAP-STATE-TIGHT IS 'byte-identical to REF (row built, dual 0)' ON NEISO AND SO 'KILLED at phase 0' IS FALSE, and the charter's case-13 rule it came from is unsound on ANY program ISO. The mass-cap row REPLACES the adder -- resolve_carbon_program returns a CarbonProgramResolution carrying EXACTLY ONE of price_adder / cap_spec (its __post_init__ invariant), so with the schedule naming NEISO the row path is taken, price_adder is None, and resolved_base_trajectory_price's row-path guard makes the resolved carbon price 0.0000 $/t in every year AGAINST REF's 26.0545 -> 34.1521. That is a resolved-INPUT delta, which is what phase 0 measures, and the charter's own gate G11 states the replace semantics that make it one. The slack test is additionally not evaluable pre-solve, because it compares the budget against emissions produced UNDER THE PRICE THE CASE REMOVES. Run neiso-2026-2030-scn-campaign-policy-2026-09-06-cap-state-tight (kind scenario), 5/5 years, 14/14 PASS. MEASURED: the row BINDS IN ALL FIVE YEARS -- emissions equal the scheduled budget to 3.2e-13 relative or better (20,670,000.000 t in 2026; 20.6700 / 20.0025 / 19.3350 / 18.6675 / 18.0000 Mt) with co2_cap_price 12.2258 / 19.0306 / 20.3238 / 12.9222 / 8.2629 $/t and n_co2_caps_binding 1 throughout -- and THE CASE NAMED 'TIGHT' IS A POLICY LOOSENING OF +2.9 TO +13.9 Mt against REF, because removing the RGGI adder raises emissions until they hit the cap and the cap stops them well above where the price instrument had them. The quantity instrument's dual is BELOW the price instrument's in every year while permitting up to 293 % more emissions. TWO STRUCTURAL READINGS ROUTED, NOT EXECUTED: (1) the cap dual reaches NO capacity screen -- evolve_fleet takes carbon_price=resolve_carbon_price(config, driver_year) = 0.0 here (runner.py:2322) and co2_cap_price has no consumer outside results/export.py and results/outputs.py -- so the campaign's one QUANTITY instrument prices dispatch while every PRICE instrument prices dispatch AND investment, and the comparison is not like-for-like; (2) that asymmetry is now visible in the deployment, not merely argued: the cap arm ends 2030 with builds_renew_mw 287.4 against REF's 1198.0 and vre_mw 6189.4 against 7100.0 -- it caps emissions and simultaneously builds LESS clean capacity than the price arm. Leakage cuts the same way: import_co2_mt_reported FALLS 0.53-0.94 Mt in every year as unpriced domestic gas undercuts imports, so the 2026 leakage-inclusive total goes 20.37 -> 24.26 Mt. COST, for the D-5 table: 72.9 min for 5 solve-years (14.57 min/solve-year) against 1.05-3.09 for every other arm in the lane -- a BINDING annual mass-cap row is an order of magnitude more expensive than an escaping clean-tier row. OWNER RULING S17 (2026-09-07, SCN-DESK r#19 card D-13, decided ON THE EVIDENCE IN THIS CELL): THE CASE IS ROUTED TO STAGE B, NOT KILLED AND NOT WITHDRAWN. The desk recorded this lane's refusal of the charter-ordered kill as the right call and took the result as card D-13; the owner then moved CAP-STATE-TIGHT OUT of the Stage-A case set, to be re-asked at a full horizon where its 2050 glide has room to bite, leaving Stage A a clean price-only policy axis. THREE things are explicitly unchanged: ruling S12's 80 %-decline slope, mass_cap_tons_by_year and the case definition all STAND as built (only the STAGE moved); the registered leg neiso-2026-2030-scn-campaign-policy-2026-09-06-cap-state-tight STAYS REGISTERED (un-registering would strand a bundle and redden the parity gate, and git history is the record either way); and every measurement above stands as the STAGE-B SEED evidence, carried intact in docs/handoffs/FINDING-scn-ws5a-policy-neiso-2026-09-07.md SS8. What the fold changes is only where the numbers are published: the case leaves the Stage-A headline, the FINDING's SS2 delta table and the readiness plan's SS5.1 rows 3 and 7, and is named in those rows as deliberately absent so no reader concludes it went unsolved. fc STAYS O -- the mechanism is neither armed nor rejected; it is a scenario case awaiting a longer horizon. Carried forward to Stage B with it: the SS7 item 2 asymmetry (the cap dual reaches no capacity screen), which a longer horizon makes worse rather than better; the cost measurement (14.57 min/solve-year, an order of magnitude above every escaping clean-tier row in the lane), which a 25-year run must be budgeted for; and the recommendation NOT to inherit the name -- the case is called TIGHT and, in this window, is not. SCN-WS5B-NEISO (2026-09-08, owner rulings S18 + S21; docs/handoffs/FINDING-scn-ws5b-neiso-2026-09-08.md, pre-registered in PRECOMMIT-scn-ws5b-neiso-2026-09-07.md + ADDENDUM-1) -- THE 25-YEAR HORIZON, 2026-2050. THE LONGER HORIZON THIS CELL WAS WAITING FOR HAS BEEN RUN, AND IT REVERSES THE READING WITHOUT RETRACTING THE STAGE-A MEASUREMENT. Run neiso-2026-2050-scn-campaign-stageb-2026-09-07-cap-state-tight, key 9bceb08bc291fced, 25/25 years, 237.2 min (14.57 min/solve-year in Stage A -> 9.49 measured here; the budget carried forward was 1.5x too pessimistic). GATE I passes with EXACT byte-identity on all six metrics against the committed Stage-A bundle. GATE III's binding limbs are READ FROM THE COMMITTED SUMMARY rather than scored by identity, which SCN-FIX3's per-year co2_cap_price makes possible, and both halves hold exactly: the cap BINDS IN 23 OF 25 YEARS with emissions equal to the budget, and is slack in exactly two (2032: 16.3734 vs 16.680; 2033: 15.8264 vs 16.020) where co2_cap_price is 0.0 EXACTLY. THE DUAL'S PATH IS THE FINDING: 12.23 -> 2.75 (2031) -> 38.00 (2040) -> 95.87 (2041) -> 5337.55 (2042), holding near 5400 to 2050, with lw_price stepping 78 -> 1688 $/MWh in the same year. FROM 2042 THE CAP IS MET ONLY BY SHEDDING LOAD: invariant I3 records unserved energy at 1.88 % of load (1199 h) in 2042 rising monotonically to 13.29 % by 2049 -- declared in the registration commit and diagnosed as this leg's RESULT, not a defect in it. THE MECHANISM IS IN THE FLEET: the case REPLACES the RGGI adder with the mass row (carbon_price_path zero), so no marginal carbon signal makes a retrofit economic and the arm builds 863.2 MW of gas_cc_ccs in 2029-30 and ZERO in every other year, against REF's 7691.3 MW at 2030 -- the loosening Stage A measured is what BUILDS THE FLEET THAT CANNOT COMPLY LATER. OVER 2026-2050 THE MASS CAP PERMITS 313.72 Mt AGAINST THE PRICE CASE'S 122.81 Mt (2.6x) while REF, on the RGGI price alone, runs 2.8-3.6 Mt through the 2030s and 40s -- three to five times BELOW the same budget -- and never sheds a MWh. Pre-registered GATE II (first year cap(y) < REF_CO2(y)) lands on 2049, EXACTLY the pre-registered point estimate, inside the 2048-2050 band. Ruling S12's 80 % slope and mass_cap_tons_by_year are NOT re-levelled by this lane: the finding is about the instrument's FORM (a quantity row replacing a price), not its level. The SS7 item 2 asymmetry carried forward from Stage A (the cap dual reaches no capacity screen) is CONFIRMED WORSE on the longer horizon and is the proximate reason the arm cannot build its way out. fc STAYS O -- a scenario case, neither armed nor rejected; the name TIGHT is now earned from 2042 and was not in the Stage-A window." },
